{%- comment -%}
  dm-mobile-fixes — small, targeted MOBILE-ONLY CSS overrides (<=767px), so
  desktop rendering is never touched. ~95% of Daisy Maison traffic is mobile.

  Fix 1 (iOS auto-zoom): personalisation text inputs render at 14px (Globo app
  default) / 13.5px (our gift-note field). iOS Safari auto-zooms the page when a
  field with font-size < 16px is focused, which jars the customer on EVERY tap
  into a builder field. Raising these to 16px on phones stops the zoom. This is
  the single highest-friction mobile issue on the personalisation flow.

  Also hosts the gift-wrap-kits registry render (product pages only) because
  layout/theme.liquid renders this snippet in <head> after daisy-cart-submit.js
  and before every product builder — exactly the load order the wrap-kit
  script needs. Move the render into theme.liquid the next time that file is
  edited; nothing else depends on it living here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .gpo-input,
  .gpo-text,
  .gpo-textarea,
  .gpo-dimension-input,
  .dm-gn-text,
  .daisy-street-options__field input[type="text"],
  .daisy-street-options__field textarea {
    font-size: 16px !important;
  }
}
</style>
{%- comment -%}
  Cookie banner (all screen sizes): assets/custom.css restyles Shopify's banner
  cream with dark text but missed the heading and the Privacy Policy link, which
  stayed Shopify's white and were invisible on cream. Move into custom.css next
  time that file is edited.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
#shopify-pc__banner h2,
.shopify-pc__banner h2,
#shopify-pc__banner .shopify-pc__banner__body a,
.shopify-pc__banner .shopify-pc__banner__body a {
  color: #2b2b2b !important;
}
</style>
{%- comment -%}
  Add-to-cart guard (product pages, all screen sizes): Globo Product Options
  still renders its hidden option set on products that now use our own
  builders (street signs, pebble pictures, etc.). Since Globo's Oct 2026
  update it listens for clicks on the whole window and, because its hidden
  required fields are empty, cancels the main "Add to cart" tap before our
  builder sees it (the sticky button was unaffected). When Globo's form is
  not visible, this marks the tapped button with Globo's own opt-out
  (.gpo-exclude / egw-atc-override) just before the click, so Globo ignores
  it. Products where Globo is visible are untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
<script>
(function(){
  function globoHidden(){
    var apps=document.querySelectorAll('.gpo-app');
    if(!apps.length)return false;
    for(var i=0;i<apps.length;i++){if(apps[i].getClientRects().length&&!apps[i].closest('[hidden]'))return false;}
    return true;
  }
  function mark(event){
    var t=event.target;if(t&&t.nodeType!==1)t=t.parentElement;
    var b=t&&t.closest&&t.closest('#product-add-to-cart,.dm-sticky-btn,button[name="add"],[type="submit"]');
    if(!b||b.closest('.gpo-app')||!globoHidden())return;
    b.classList.add('gpo-exclude');b.setAttribute('egw-atc-override','');
  }
  ['pointerdown','touchstart','mousedown','keydown','click'].forEach(function(type){
    window.addEventListener(type,mark,{capture:true,passive:true});
  });
})();
</script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}{% render 'dm-wrap-kits' %}{%- endif -%}